WEBVTT

01:31.007 --> 01:32.007
VERDIGRIS HOUSE

01:32.008 --> 01:34.009
THIS STORY IS A FICTION AND ALL NAMES OF
FIGURES AND ORGANIZATIONS ARE FICTITIOUS.

01:34.010 --> 01:34.928
MOREOVER, THE STORY HAS NO RELATION
TO REAL-LIFE INCIDENTS AND EVENTS.

01:40.016 --> 01:41.267
Greetings.

01:42.727 --> 01:45.145
Now there's a face I didn't expect to see.

01:45.146 --> 01:47.648
You, of all people?

01:47.649 --> 01:49.901
What a rude thing to say.

01:55.698 --> 01:57.157
<i>This guy is Lahan.</i>

01:57.158 --> 02:00.869
<i>He's from the La clan,
which is obvious from his name.</i>

02:00.870 --> 02:04.124
<i>He's the nephew and adopted son
of that weirdo strategist.</i>

02:04.707 --> 02:07.460
I didn't know you liked street performers.

02:08.044 --> 02:13.049
Well, even I get curious
when everyone's buzzing about something.

02:15.426 --> 02:19.930
I hear this girl with albinism
is quite the beauty.

02:19.931 --> 02:23.767
<i>I forgot that this man
has a weakness for objects of beauty.</i>

02:23.768 --> 02:27.814
<i>But unlike most people,
he supposedly sees beauty as numbers.</i>

02:28.398 --> 02:30.692
<i>That weirdo's adopted son
is a weirdo himself.</i>

02:31.359 --> 02:34.111
So you came to invite me?

02:34.112 --> 02:35.989
You're curious too, right?

02:36.489 --> 02:37.739
I won't deny it.

02:37.740 --> 02:41.910
<i>Does this guy have anything to gain
from inviting me, though?</i>

02:41.911 --> 02:45.414
<i>Is he trying to curry favor
with the weirdo strategist?</i>

02:45.415 --> 02:47.166
Father isn't here, you know.

02:47.167 --> 02:48.166
Really?

02:48.167 --> 02:49.586
His subordinate is, though.

02:51.921 --> 02:54.299
Don't give me that look.
You see, Sir Laka--

02:57.552 --> 03:00.889
I'll address him as "Master Strategist."
No problem there, right?

03:02.682 --> 03:05.184
I'm Rikuson,
Master Strategist's subordinate.

03:06.436 --> 03:07.562
I'm Maomao.

03:08.146 --> 03:09.397
I'm well aware.

03:10.231 --> 03:12.650
Why'd he send a subordinate in his place?

03:13.610 --> 03:17.322
<i>Father probably won't leave
the residence for a while, you see.</i>

03:17.822 --> 03:21.451
Okay, so why'd you invite me?

03:22.410 --> 03:26.079
<i>Lahan would never invite me
without weighing the pros and cons.</i>

03:26.080 --> 03:28.040
<i>If my memory serves me right,</i>

03:28.041 --> 03:30.626
<i>he's almost as miserly as Grams.</i>

03:30.627 --> 03:33.338
This time, I've got business in the West.

03:33.922 --> 03:38.176
I might ask that traveling entertainer
to perform at a banquet.

03:38.676 --> 03:39.593
And?

03:39.594 --> 03:42.763
Some of their guests are female, you see.

03:42.764 --> 03:45.390
I'd like your opinion
from that perspective.

03:45.391 --> 03:46.434
Liar.

03:48.311 --> 03:50.229
<i>What an annoying pose.</i>

03:50.230 --> 03:55.526
My boss, Master Strategist,
actually made a comment about this.

03:57.403 --> 03:58.780
Curious, indeed...

04:00.865 --> 04:02.282
That's all he said.

04:02.283 --> 04:05.452
<i>There's no basis
for anything that weirdo strategist says.</i>

04:05.453 --> 04:08.789
<i>If anything,
it's just supernatural intuition.</i>

04:08.790 --> 04:12.167
Just in case, I investigated
those traveling entertainers.

04:12.168 --> 04:14.962
Then, I caught wind of a certain rumor.

04:14.963 --> 04:15.797
Rumor?

04:16.464 --> 04:17.298
Yes.

04:24.180 --> 04:26.849
I hope this doesn't inconvenience me.

04:30.728 --> 04:32.021
Shall we depart?

04:37.902 --> 04:42.990
<i>The immortal maiden's theater is located
in the capital's most prosperous district.</i>

04:42.991 --> 04:45.492
<i>With high-class residences nearby,</i>

04:45.493 --> 04:49.663
<i>it's strange that they're holding
solo performances there.</i>

04:49.664 --> 04:53.584
<i>Moreover, the immortal's appearance
earned her the nickname, "White Lady."</i>

04:54.127 --> 04:55.669
<i>Also, "White Goddess."</i>

04:55.670 --> 04:58.756
<i>That's an ambitious name
for a mere traveling entertainer.</i>

04:59.257 --> 05:01.968
For an immortal maiden,
she sounds pretty mortal.

05:02.927 --> 05:04.178
We've arrived.

05:09.517 --> 05:10.393
Thank you.

05:10.893 --> 05:12.394
What's all this for?

05:12.395 --> 05:15.230
Events like this are quite lowly, you see.

05:15.231 --> 05:18.483
These small touches help us
pretend we don't know each other.

05:18.484 --> 05:20.653
That makes things smoother.

05:25.783 --> 05:29.203
<i>Traveling entertainers
performing in such a fancy theater?</i>

05:29.704 --> 05:31.456
<i>She's got sponsors, no doubt.</i>

05:31.956 --> 05:33.499
Our seats are over there.

05:37.712 --> 05:41.007
Sir Jinshi, you didn't need
to come here in person.

05:41.507 --> 05:44.051
I might as well. It's a rare opportunity.

05:44.052 --> 05:44.886
But...

05:45.511 --> 05:48.389
I want to see this White Lady for myself.

05:49.515 --> 05:51.183
Here's our table.

05:51.184 --> 05:53.435
The center tables were in high demand

05:53.436 --> 05:55.563
and unnecessarily pricey...

05:57.356 --> 05:59.067
Exactly, exactly.

05:59.734 --> 06:01.152
Here you are.

06:02.653 --> 06:05.363
<i>Baked sweets served with alcohol?</i>

06:05.364 --> 06:07.617
<i>Strange combination.</i>

06:11.537 --> 06:13.289
You're not guzzling the alcohol?

06:13.873 --> 06:15.291
<i>I love me some booze, but...</i>

06:16.084 --> 06:17.335
I'll drink it later.

06:17.835 --> 06:20.295
Or did you want me to check for poison?

06:20.296 --> 06:21.422
No, it's fine.

06:21.923 --> 06:23.256
You're not drinking?

06:23.257 --> 06:26.635
I can't be the only one acting a fool.

06:26.636 --> 06:28.804
Yes, this pairs well.

06:28.805 --> 06:30.264
An unusual flavor.

06:57.583 --> 06:59.835
<i>So, that's the White Lady.</i>

06:59.836 --> 07:05.424
<i>Skin tone aside, that demeanor of hers...
Could she be from the West?</i>

07:19.564 --> 07:22.608
Now, who's occupying this table?

07:23.276 --> 07:24.484
That's us.

07:24.485 --> 07:25.528
It's us, all right.

07:26.028 --> 07:27.320
What should we do?

07:27.321 --> 07:29.489
That's not for me to decide.

07:29.490 --> 07:31.242
Why don't you go?

07:31.951 --> 07:34.036
It's a chance to watch up close.

07:36.205 --> 07:37.915
Okay, I'll go.

07:40.835 --> 07:41.919
<i>Is that...</i>

07:46.591 --> 07:48.801
<i>No, it couldn't be.</i>

07:53.306 --> 07:56.057
<i>Transparent skin
with blood vessels showing through.</i>

07:56.058 --> 07:58.519
<i>It's different from white face powder.</i>

07:59.187 --> 08:02.148
Write any number you'd like, please.

08:02.773 --> 08:05.526
"Write any number you'd like, please!"

08:08.488 --> 08:11.156
Make sure I can't see it,

08:11.157 --> 08:15.036
and fold it up small
so that nobody else can see it either.

08:22.668 --> 08:24.462
<i>Write on this paper, huh?</i>

08:24.962 --> 08:28.549
<i>There's even a pad underneath
to avoid staining the desk.</i>

08:31.052 --> 08:35.348
<i>It's hard to write
with all this excess ink...</i>

08:36.140 --> 08:39.684
<i>It's a little gritty, too.
They should've mixed it better.</i>

08:39.685 --> 08:40.686
SEVEN

08:43.439 --> 08:44.565
Finished.

08:52.031 --> 08:55.701
Could you insert that paper
into one of these tubes?

08:56.369 --> 08:59.747
When you're done,
please pull the cloth over.

09:07.838 --> 09:08.839
Finished.

09:40.788 --> 09:43.540
<i>She doesn't have good eyesight.</i>

09:43.541 --> 09:46.586
You wrote the number 7, didn't you?

09:50.631 --> 09:51.757
Bingo.

09:56.262 --> 09:57.430
<i>She reminds me</i>

09:58.014 --> 09:59.390
<i>of a white snake.</i>

10:01.601 --> 10:04.145
It's a messenger of God, so don't kill it.

10:05.187 --> 10:07.481
<i>It's got nothing to do with God.</i>

10:07.982 --> 10:12.278
<i>I hate it when my old man
tries to be all ethical sometimes.</i>

10:13.154 --> 10:15.196
<i>It's strangely hot.</i>

10:15.197 --> 10:16.699
<i>My head hurts, too.</i>

10:17.450 --> 10:20.077
<i>Feels like
mosquitoes are buzzing around my ears.</i>

10:23.789 --> 10:25.499
The tube you selected

10:26.000 --> 10:29.670
was third from the top,
second from the left.

10:33.215 --> 10:34.258
Correct?

10:38.763 --> 10:43.017
Third from the top,
second from the left. This one!

10:49.065 --> 10:50.815
She wrote "Seven."

10:50.816 --> 10:52.442
It's really seven!

10:52.443 --> 10:54.612
She even chose the correct slot!

10:55.196 --> 10:56.906
How did she do that?

10:58.324 --> 11:02.370
<i>I'd bet Maomao
could figure this trick out too.</i>

11:02.953 --> 11:05.413
So, what happened?

11:05.414 --> 11:07.248
What do you mean, "What happened?"

11:07.249 --> 11:11.211
Did somebody bribe you
to do that or something?

11:11.212 --> 11:12.796
Unlike you, I'd never do that.

11:12.797 --> 11:16.300
Neither would I.
How unsightly that would be...

11:16.884 --> 11:18.802
Was anyone watching you?

11:18.803 --> 11:20.971
I don't think anyone saw me.

11:21.806 --> 11:25.476
<i>The only ones on stage
were the White Lady and her helper boy.</i>

11:25.976 --> 11:27.977
<i>They couldn't see my number.</i>

11:27.978 --> 11:32.316
<i>And that cloth I pulled over
should've concealed the tube I chose.</i>

11:33.025 --> 11:35.403
<i>Perhaps it was a mirror?</i>

11:36.112 --> 11:40.532
<i>No, it should've been too hazy
to see anything in that dim light.</i>

11:40.533 --> 11:42.283
<i>It would fog the mirror.</i>

11:42.284 --> 11:45.287
<i>Besides, it seemed like
the White Lady had poor eyesight.</i>

11:45.830 --> 11:48.790
<i>Even up close,
everything should be blurry.</i>

11:48.791 --> 11:50.292
<i>So how on earth...</i>

11:57.258 --> 11:59.134
Just a piece of copper, right?

11:59.135 --> 12:00.594
Yeah, no doubt.

12:28.289 --> 12:29.664
<i>It changed color.</i>

12:29.665 --> 12:31.499
The copper turned to silver!

12:31.500 --> 12:32.959
Let me see!

12:32.960 --> 12:34.462
It's definitely silver.

12:45.639 --> 12:47.265
The silver changed to gold!

12:47.266 --> 12:49.058
That's impossible!

12:49.059 --> 12:49.894
Basen.

12:50.728 --> 12:51.770
I'm terribly sorry.

12:55.608 --> 12:57.317
Can you explain this?

12:57.318 --> 12:58.443
Later.

12:58.444 --> 13:00.863
For now, let me enjoy the show.

13:27.014 --> 13:29.098
Silver-colored liquid?

13:29.099 --> 13:30.226
What is it?

13:33.270 --> 13:34.897
She's not gonna...

13:41.654 --> 13:43.989
Did you have another enjoyable night?

13:44.907 --> 13:46.991
I do hope we meet again.

13:46.992 --> 13:48.826
Astounding sorcery.

13:48.827 --> 13:50.412
It's the real deal!

13:51.664 --> 13:53.122
My dear White Lady...

13:53.123 --> 13:55.251
Is that real sorcery?

13:55.834 --> 13:57.795
There must be a trick to it.

13:58.462 --> 13:59.504
We're leaving.

13:59.505 --> 14:00.506
Yes, sir.

14:01.090 --> 14:04.634
Also, investigate the high officials
who frequent this place.

14:04.635 --> 14:05.469
As you wish.

14:06.262 --> 14:09.223
<i>That White Lady is a threat.</i>

14:14.728 --> 14:16.480
There's something unusual about this...

14:18.649 --> 14:19.608
Is something wrong?

14:20.234 --> 14:21.193
Yeah.

14:27.658 --> 14:29.785
Tastes like there's something mixed in.

14:32.162 --> 14:34.038
<i>Not much alcohol.</i>

14:34.039 --> 14:35.915
<i>Like juice, it's easy to drink.</i>

14:35.916 --> 14:37.918
<i>But the taste is vaguely complex.</i>

14:38.544 --> 14:41.004
<i>There's a little salt in it.</i>

14:41.005 --> 14:45.217
It's not poison, but they've altered it
to enhance the alcohol's effects.

14:46.176 --> 14:47.635
<i>On top of that,</i>

14:47.636 --> 14:51.181
<i>the dim room
with gently swaying paper lanterns.</i>

14:52.224 --> 14:55.352
<i>A mysterious haze and an ethereal maiden.</i>

14:55.936 --> 14:58.730
<i>Inexplicable phenomena
unfolding before our very eyes.</i>

14:58.731 --> 15:02.192
<i>Wouldn't that be enough
to put blind faith in her?</i>

15:03.736 --> 15:05.737
<i>Just as I thought. A little salty.</i>

15:05.738 --> 15:07.573
<i>It would taste better without it.</i>

15:12.244 --> 15:13.203
What are you doing?

15:13.829 --> 15:15.539
This is how she did it.

15:16.123 --> 15:19.627
<i>If she pulled this off,
there must be a trick to that, too.</i>

15:20.252 --> 15:24.423
<i>The haze was relatively thick
and hot enough to induce a headache,</i>

15:25.007 --> 15:27.176
<i>which somehow broke my concentration.</i>

15:28.052 --> 15:29.094
<i>The haze...</i>

15:29.637 --> 15:31.221
<i>Could that be vapor?</i>

15:31.889 --> 15:34.933
<i>Pumping out steam
from behind the stage, maybe?</i>

15:34.934 --> 15:36.810
<i>That would explain the heat.</i>

15:37.519 --> 15:39.396
<i>Then, why did my head hurt?</i>

15:39.897 --> 15:42.191
<i>It felt like mosquitoes buzzing.</i>

15:42.900 --> 15:44.401
<i>Could it have been...</i>

15:49.740 --> 15:54.912
What are you whistling for?
It's crude to taunt like that.

15:59.708 --> 16:02.252
<i>Okay, I know what's up.</i>

16:09.760 --> 16:12.303
This fancy booze hits different.

16:12.304 --> 16:14.722
Have you no restraint whatsoever?

16:14.723 --> 16:16.849
You're well-paid. What's the problem?

16:16.850 --> 16:20.603
We made expensive purchases
at the Verdigris House last year.

16:20.604 --> 16:21.896
I'm broke, you know.

16:21.897 --> 16:24.024
Are you ready to tell us now?

16:25.275 --> 16:28.861
First, I'll tell you how
she turned copper into silver and gold.

16:28.862 --> 16:31.906
It's similar to what they call
"transmutation."

16:31.907 --> 16:33.116
Transmutation?

16:33.117 --> 16:36.745
It might be easier
to think of it as liandan-shu.

16:37.329 --> 16:42.083
<i>Along those lines, transmutation
involves converting nonmetals into metals.</i>

16:42.084 --> 16:43.960
It's similar to that?

16:43.961 --> 16:46.754
Yes, but if I had to compare it
to anything,

16:46.755 --> 16:50.758
I'd say it's closer
to what they call "alchemy" in the West.

16:50.759 --> 16:52.051
The West, huh?

16:52.052 --> 16:55.722
Yeah, I've only heard stories
from my old man, though.

16:55.723 --> 16:59.435
<i>It's not a matter of conversion
into silver or gold.</i>

17:00.060 --> 17:01.811
<i>Apparently, it's plating.</i>

17:01.812 --> 17:05.649
<i>They're simply heating it with fire
to change its appearance.</i>

17:06.233 --> 17:09.068
So? What do you mean, "plating"?

17:09.069 --> 17:12.947
Coating the metal
with a different kind of metal.

17:12.948 --> 17:15.450
If you wanna know more, go ask my old man.

17:15.451 --> 17:18.703
And I'd appreciate it
if you could report back to me.

17:18.704 --> 17:19.746
For real, go.

17:19.747 --> 17:20.998
What? Okay...

17:22.041 --> 17:24.584
<i>Also, the paper
spontaneously catching fire</i>

17:24.585 --> 17:27.963
<i>is possible with by-products
created during this process.</i>

17:28.547 --> 17:33.010
<i>That would explain the butterflies too,
if they were cleverly made out of paper.</i>

17:33.552 --> 17:37.055
<i>Everyone's vision
was blurred from the haze.</i>

17:37.056 --> 17:39.808
<i>They were also intoxicated from the booze.</i>

17:40.350 --> 17:43.644
<i>You guys didn't even drink,
and she still fooled you.</i>

17:43.645 --> 17:45.272
So, I doubt anyone noticed.

17:45.898 --> 17:48.984
How did she read your mind, then?

17:49.568 --> 17:50.861
I'll tell you.

17:53.405 --> 17:54.655
Paper.

17:54.656 --> 17:56.075
Someone's getting big-headed.

18:04.166 --> 18:05.918
The wet areas shrank.

18:06.418 --> 18:08.377
That's not the point.

18:08.378 --> 18:10.880
Show your dear older brother
some respect, would you?

18:10.881 --> 18:12.216
<i>Not on your life.</i>

18:13.050 --> 18:16.303
So, what does this
have to do with anything?

18:17.179 --> 18:18.639
Look here.

18:22.851 --> 18:26.104
<i>Invisible writing, revealed with heat.
I've done this before.</i>

18:26.105 --> 18:29.024
<i>Sir Jinshi would've noticed
without me explaining it.</i>

18:29.650 --> 18:30.566
Does that help?

18:30.567 --> 18:32.485
It doesn't answer my question.

18:32.486 --> 18:35.114
How does this relate to reading minds?

18:36.532 --> 18:37.574
How does it taste?

18:38.283 --> 18:41.661
Tastes like seafood broth,
but it's a little salty.

18:41.662 --> 18:43.371
That means it contains salt.

18:43.372 --> 18:44.580
Yeah, so?

18:44.581 --> 18:47.626
The ink on my brush also contained salt.

18:48.127 --> 18:51.587
No wonder it was gritty
and difficult to write with.

18:51.588 --> 18:53.798
So they applied heat to see your number?

18:53.799 --> 18:56.009
No, there are other ways to see it.

18:56.844 --> 18:59.720
<i>There was a black pad under my paper.</i>

18:59.721 --> 19:03.349
<i>The salty ink must have bled into that.</i>

19:03.350 --> 19:05.017
That's how she did it?

19:05.018 --> 19:06.269
Makes sense.

19:06.270 --> 19:10.315
So, how did she know
which tube you stuck the paper through?

19:12.484 --> 19:14.862
Even you know how flutes work, right?

19:15.571 --> 19:17.781
You blow it to produce sound...

19:21.076 --> 19:22.368
And to change the sound?

19:22.369 --> 19:25.538
You change the number of holes
your breath passes through.

19:25.539 --> 19:27.207
Even I know that.

19:27.791 --> 19:32.920
<i>What if the tube containing my paper
acted just like the hole of a flute?</i>

19:32.921 --> 19:35.924
<i>Flute? I didn't hear anything like that...</i>

19:36.633 --> 19:40.344
<i>Hiding among the bells
and gongs in that theater,</i>

19:40.345 --> 19:42.556
<i>there was another important sound.</i>

19:43.390 --> 19:47.102
I think it was a high-pitched sound
that went unnoticed.

19:47.686 --> 19:48.936
High-pitched?

19:48.937 --> 19:52.648
Yes, high-pitched sounds cause headaches.

19:52.649 --> 19:54.692
I may not have recognized the sound,

19:54.693 --> 19:57.029
but I unconsciously felt some discomfort.

19:59.448 --> 20:00.990
I can hear that.

20:00.991 --> 20:01.867
How about this?

20:03.827 --> 20:04.995
I can still hear it.

20:05.579 --> 20:07.247
I kind of hear it.

20:08.290 --> 20:09.707
I can't.

20:09.708 --> 20:11.209
Good.

20:11.210 --> 20:14.004
Sounds like these
become less audible with age.

20:15.631 --> 20:19.218
<i>That immortal maiden
had incredibly sensitive ears.</i>

20:19.885 --> 20:23.764
Basically, the sound of a flute
led her to the correct tube?

20:24.348 --> 20:28.601
Yeah, the flute sounded
to the rhythm of the gongs and bells.

20:28.602 --> 20:31.313
If she can tell about ten pitches apart,
that should be enough.

20:31.813 --> 20:33.273
But how did they blow on it?

20:33.857 --> 20:36.777
<i>That can be explained by the haze.</i>

20:37.569 --> 20:41.949
<i>I'm guessing the haze was vapor.
They fed steam underneath the desk.</i>

20:43.867 --> 20:45.869
Are you convinced now?

20:48.622 --> 20:53.626
Lastly, about that silver liquid
the White Lady drank.

20:53.627 --> 20:55.211
It was mercury.

20:55.212 --> 20:56.338
A deadly poison.

20:57.130 --> 21:00.300
I dunno if she really drank it,
but don't try that at home.

21:01.134 --> 21:04.304
You should explain this
to the high officials sometime.

21:09.977 --> 21:11.811
<i>The White Lady's show and her crew</i>

21:11.812 --> 21:15.232
<i>vanished without a trace just days later.</i>

21:16.108 --> 21:17.817
<i>Instead, what remained</i>

21:17.818 --> 21:21.738
<i>were mysterious cases
of food poisoning among capital merchants.</i>

21:22.906 --> 21:26.994
<i>An immortal maiden like a white snake.
What was she trying to accomplish?</i>

21:27.828 --> 21:30.121
<i>Inhaling mercury through steam</i>

21:30.122 --> 21:33.834
<i>or sticking it on other objects
to alter their form is highly toxic.</i>

21:36.253 --> 21:40.173
<i>However, it's also used
as medicine sometimes.</i>

21:48.724 --> 21:50.225
<i>With poison and medicine,</i>

21:51.685 --> 21:53.520
<i>it's all about how you use them.</i>

